[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 457,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 370,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64805,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 338,
        "headingId": 370,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Villous adenoma of the vagina is a primary vaginal benign glandular tumour with villiform and/or tubular structures lined by intestinal-type columnar epithelium with pseudostratified elongated hyperchromatic nuclei.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:04:09"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 458,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 371,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64806,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 338,
        "headingId": 371,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8261/0 Villous adenoma NOS</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:04:09"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 459,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 372,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64807,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 338,
        "headingId": 372,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2F33.Y &amp; XH90D6 Benign neoplasm of other specified female genital organs &amp; Villous adenoma NOS</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:04:09"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 460,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 373,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64808,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 338,
        "headingId": 373,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> tubulovillous adenoma; intestinal-type adenoma; adenomatous polyp</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:04:09"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 461,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 374,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64809,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 338,
        "headingId": 374,
        "headingText": "<p>None</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-07-22T12:23:37"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 462,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 375,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64810,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 338,
        "headingId": 375,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Various locations within the vagina have been reported {24722061}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:04:09"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 463,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 376,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64811,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 338,
        "headingId": 376,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Villous adenomas of the vagina have been reported in adults aged 19&ndash;80&nbsp;years {24722061; 23202776}. Most patients present with a vaginal mass or abnormal vaginal bleeding {24722061}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:04:09"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 464,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 377,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64812,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 338,
        "headingId": 377,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These are extremely rare vaginal lesions.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:04:09"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 465,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 378,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64813,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 338,
        "headingId": 378,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Speculated origins include intestinal metaplasia of the vaginal surface epithelium or adenosis, congenital rests of intestinal epithelium (cloacal remnants), and extension of intestinal epithelium through a rectovaginal fistula {24722061}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:04:09"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 466,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 379,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64814,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 338,
        "headingId": 379,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>An activating mutation in <em>KRAS</em> and a frameshift truncating mutation in <em>APC</em> were demonstrated in one case {30383609}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:04:09"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64815,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 338,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These are polypoid lesions, with reported cases measuring 0.9&ndash;3&nbsp;cm {24722061; 23202776}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:04:09"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64816,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 338,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Histology shows villiform and/or tubular structures lined by columnar epithelium with atypical pseudostratified elongated hyperchromatic nuclei, often containing scattered goblet cells {24722061}. No stromal invasion is present. Cases with significant nuclear atypia and/or architectural complexity should be diagnosed as adenomas with high-grade dysplasia using the criteria applicable to their colorectal counterparts {24722061}. Immunohistochemically, they are usually positive for CK20 and CDX2; CK7 is variable {24722061; 30383609}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:04:09"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 468,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 381,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64817,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 338,
        "headingId": 381,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:04:09"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 469,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 382,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64818,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 338,
        "headingId": 382,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:04:09"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 472,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 385,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64819,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 338,
        "headingId": 385,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> tubulovillous/villous architecture; intestinal-type epithelium with nuclear pseudostratification and hyperchromasia; no stromal invasion.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> presence of goblet cells; positivity for CK20 and/or CDX2.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:04:09"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 470,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 383,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64820,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 338,
        "headingId": 383,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:04:09"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 471,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 384,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64821,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 338,
        "headingId": 384,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>In some reported cases with follow-up, the follow-up was uneventful; in others, neoplasms recurred {24722061; 15661252}. One patient developed intestinal-type adenocarcinoma 2&nbsp;years after diagnosis of adenoma with high-grade dysplasia {24722061}. Metachronous vulvar tubulovillous adenoma was reported in one case {30383609}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:04:09"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]